'' A '#cmdline' '-Wl' is held to linker options that change only the program. '-plugin' runs
'' code inside GNU ld, and '@file' is a response file of anything at all; both are refused,
'' and so is lld-link's '/OUT'; the '-rpath' and '/STACK' beside them are not.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --parse-only tests/driver/src/cmdline-wl-plugin.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: error TKO0178: '-Wl' is not allowed in a #cmdline: the linker option '-plugin' is not one a source may pass
'' EXPECT-OUT: error TKO0178: '-Wl' is not allowed in a #cmdline: '@cmdline-args.rsp' would reach the linker as a response file
'' EXPECT-NOT: -rpath
'' EXPECT-OUT: error TKO0178: '-Wl' is not allowed in a #cmdline: the linker option '/OUT:C:/evil.exe' is not one a source may pass
'' EXPECT-NOT: STACK
